        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0010" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg4"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.24/41: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Des Fortes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-06-28T17:00:00-06:00">June 28, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Department’s circular June 27, 7 p.m. I have taken up the subject matter of
                    the Department’s instruction with the Foreign Minister who viewed it very
                    sympathetically. The Foreign Minister is referring it to the President upon the
                    latter’s return.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Des Portes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
